# Check everything out with LF endings, on every platform.
#
# Git's default on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which
# changes the bytes of files bough embeds (//go:embed) and compares —
# the /init template's own test failed on windows-latest for exactly
# that reason, matching "verified by\n  running them" against text the
# checkout had turned into "\r\n". Go tooling wants LF regardless.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: these are bytes, not text.
*.png binary
*.gz binary
*.ico binary
